Código Penal and CPC verified 2026-10-28: replays of Planalto's annotated del2848.htm and l13105.htm match del2848compilado.htm / l13105compilada.htm except typesetting-only differences between the two official pages (CP 25 articles, CPC 1 article; listed in decisions); 0 replay problems; in-force days from each amending law's own clause or LINDB; check.py 0 mismatches; parse deterministic and --compare history identical. Re-verified 2026-10-31 after the stale-wording fixes of batch7/stale_fix.py (run through batch7/oldparts.py 60-phase2): where Planalto's page settles it, two wordings of one dispositivo no longer stand at once (each case listed in decisions); a duplicate-label check over every version is clean; the replay check against Planalto's consolidated or annotated page is unchanged; merged scratch build 998 commits, 33 acts, check.py 0 mismatches, 0 trailer errors, --compare history identical; part sha256 511b729f. Re-verified 2026-10-31 ~04:58Z after the quoted-amendment fix (lines closing an amendment quoted from another law, such as '....." (NR)', stay in the article that quotes them instead of moving into the next article; shared parsers proc/parse_proc.py, parse_phase2.py, clt/parse_clt.py): CPC arts. 1.060, 1.064, 1.065 and 1.068 (closing lines of the quoted Lei 9.099 and Código Eleitoral amendments, until now filed under arts. 1.061-1.069). Every version holds the same lines as before (only their article changed); today's text otherwise unchanged and still matches Planalto as listed above; dup/leak checks unchanged; merged scratch build 61 acts, 1595 versions, 1433 commits, check.py 0 mismatches, 0 trailer errors, --compare identical, audit_push clean; part sha256 abba1d64.
Effect days reviewed 2026-10-31 (coordinator rule: a change whose act fixes a later 'produção de efeitos' day is dated by that day): the deferred-effects clauses this part lists are retroactive, financial only, conditional (a later act, regulation or ministerial attestation) or name provisions other than the ones this part's acts received, so no version moves; only the decision stating the dating rule was reworded (effects_fix.py; history, laws and credits byte-identical). Part sha256 90d5561e; merged scratch build 112 acts, 2056 versions, 1744 commits, check.py 0 mismatches, 0 trailer errors, --compare identical, audit_push clean.
